Minimum operation to make all elements equal in array

Given an array consisting of n positive integers, the task is to find the minimum number of operations to make all elements equal. 
In each operation, we can perform addition, multiplication, subtraction, or division with any number and an array element. 

Explanaton:

The key idea 🧠:  You can change any one element in exactly 1 operation to become whatever value you want.
So the question becomes: Which value already appears the most times?
Because we should keep those elements unchanged and modify everything else.

Code:

static int minOperations(int[] arr) {
        int n = arr.length;
        // Maximum possible operations would be n
        int minOps = n;

        // Try each element as the potential final value
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int currOps = 0;

            // Count how many elements are different from
            // arr[i]
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                if (arr[i] != arr[j]) {
                    currOps++;
                }
            }

            // Update minimum operations
            minOps = Math.min(minOps, currOps);
        }

        return minOps;
    }
